        "original_id": "b6624713-1e93-575b-a458-8a9bd2bbb87c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Simon Grundel-Helmfelt, Charles XI of Sweden\n- Events: Battle of Lund, Scanian War\n- Places: Lund, Scania, Sweden\n\nFacts:\n- The Battle of Lund, part of the Scanian War, was fought on December 4, 1676, north of the city of Lund in Scania in southern Sweden.\n- The Battle of Lund was fought between the invading Danish army and the army of Charles XI of Sweden.\n- Simon Grundel-Helmfelt is most notable for his overwhelming victory at the Battle of Lund despite being heavily outnumbered by Danish troops.",
